answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "nonzero for at least one $t\\in R$" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-333843/field-2" :answer-field/id #uuid "708538dc-ffcd-585d-9acc-a12ef8cbb570" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/select :answer-field/correct "q-333843/field-2/b458e7ce396e2645405ae9ea0b183f63221f0e5b935ce41459202d3714e3b25a" :answer-field/choices ["q-333843/field-2/b458e7ce396e2645405ae9ea0b183f63221f0e5b935ce41459202d3714e3b25a" "q-333843/field-2/aa8b3f9c78bb7b825079ad4aaf338d07c96e446b686a39a5121216be4228efdb"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-333843/field-3/988842f9ae7a51d1679b23c13893e9f8d3070ea423527b72c2d8836642aabb0a" :answer/id #uuid "6bc35b8b-2ef7-5beb-b61a-6e40047f0bfb" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "dependent" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-333843/field-3/a8a725fec0b63a3b8d6f4591903bfe81596da23bd6deceff5c00414df35bbd3f" :answer/id #uuid "a8a96672-6012-580f-8171-180174e0e4a2" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "independent" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-333843/field-3" :answer-field/id #uuid "f0e961ee-a2d0-5afc-b3e7-0cc9812dbe86" :answer-field/key "field-3" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/select :answer-field/correct "q-333843/field-3/988842f9ae7a51d1679b23c13893e9f8d3070ea423527b72c2d8836642aabb0a" :answer-field/choices ["q-333843/field-3/988842f9ae7a51d1679b23c13893e9f8d3070ea423527b72c2d8836642aabb0a" "q-333843/field-3/a8a725fec0b63a3b8d6f4591903bfe81596da23bd6deceff5c00414df35bbd3f"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-333843" :question/id #uuid "9ed2e684-f57d-5c2f-88f3-95cfac441d13" :question/math-academy-id "q-333843" :question/problem "$$\n{x}_{1}(t)=[\\begin{aligned}{e}^{t} \\\\ -3{e}^{t}\\end{aligned}],\\,{x}_{2}(t)=[\\begin{aligned}-2{e}^{t} \\\\ 6{e}^{t}\\end{aligned}],\\,t\\in R\n$$\n\nConsider the vector-valued functions ${x}_{1}(t)$ and ${x}_{2}(t)$ above. Given that ${x}_{1}$ and ${x}_{2}$ are solutions of the same system of linear ODEs, select the correct options in the reasoning below.$\\,$ The Wronskian is $W({x}_{1},{x}_{2})=$ \n{{field-1}},\nwhich is\n{{field-2}}.  \n\n$\\,$ Therefore, the set ${{x}_{1}(t),{x}_{2}(t)}$ is linearly \n{{field-3}} \non $R.$" :question/worked-solution "The Wronskian $W({x}_{1},{x}_{2})$ of two vector-valued functions \n\n$$\n{x}_{1}(t)=[\\begin{aligned}{x}_{11}(t) \\\\ {x}_{21}(t)\\end{aligned}],\\,{x}_{2}(t)=[\\begin{aligned}{x}_{12}(t) \\\\ {x}_{22}(t)\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nis defined as\n\n$$\nW({x}_{1},{x}_{2})=det({x}_{1},{x}_{2})=|\\begin{aligned}{x}_{11}(t) & {x}_{12}(t) \\\\ {x}_{21}(t) & {x}_{22}(t)\\end{aligned}|.\n$$\n\nNote the following:\n\n- If the Wronskian is not identically zero, then ${x}_{1}$ and ${x}_{2}$ are linearly independent.\n\n- If the Wronskian is identically zero, and it's known that ${x}_{1}$ and ${x}_{2}$ are solutions to the same system of linear ODEs, then ${x}_{1}$ and ${x}_{2}$ are linearly dependent.\n\nIn our case, our Wronskian is given by\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}W({x}_{1},{x}_{2}) & =|\\begin{aligned}{e}^{t} & -2{e}^{t} \\\\ -3{e}^{t} & 6{e}^{t}\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =({e}^{t})\\cdot (6{e}^{t})-(-2{e}^{t})\\cdot (-3{e}^{t}) \\\\  & =6{e}^{2t}-6{e}^{2t} \\\\  & =0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhich is $\\text{zero for all }t\\in R.$\n\nTherefore, the set ${{x}_{1}(t),{x}_{2}(t)}$ is linearly $\\text{dependent}$ on $R.$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-333843/field-1" "q-333843/field-2" "q-333843/field-3"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "ee461d3e-3afa-51c6-bddd-355668cac3ec"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-333843"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-333863/field-1/d971375f57c56d8a55a09f2b892e108787b055ceeadf005d7beed73e388cc467" :answer/id #uuid "c62ea812-bfec-53a6-9a2b-dea6b7ddc7f0" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "0" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-333863/field-1/c5740d59e9262109ab30094e2b